From: mscharged-port
Subject: Release textures the game stops using in native GX mode
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: native host resource lifetime fix (GPU memory leak).

Aurora releases a cached texture object once it has not been bound for 600
frames, in gx::texture::end_frame(). Only the diagnostic aurora::end_frame()
calls it, and native GX recording (0033) forbids that path, so in the game the
cache's frame counter never advanced and nothing was ever released.
GXInitTexObj gives each call a new object, and the movie player prepares its
Y/U/V textures again for every decoded frame: every movie frame stayed in GPU
memory (about 1.7 GB during the credits), and new stadiums and characters added
their textures for good. A Windows player's session that ended with
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY after 19 minutes held about 6.4 GB of small
textures. The display copy now ends a native frame and ages the caches there,
on the FIFO processor that owns them. A playing movie still keeps its last 600
frames of textures (the credits level off about 1 GB above the menus).

Copied EFB textures are cached per destination, size and format. A copy to a
destination at a new size (after a window resize) or format left the older
textures allocated for good; such a copy now releases them first, as the
destination holds only its newest copy.

diff --git a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXFrameBuffer.cpp b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXFrameBuffer.cpp
index a8a3e34..844ff3a 100644
--- a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXFrameBuffer.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXFrameBuffer.cpp
@@ -52,6 +52,9 @@ void copy_tex(const void* dest, GXBool clear) noexcept {
   };
   auto it = g_gxState.copyTextureCache.find(key);
   if (it == g_gxState.copyTextureCache.end()) {
+    // A destination holds only its newest copy. Release the textures of copies
+    // made to it at another size (before a window resize) or format.
+    evict_copy_texture(dest);
     gfx::TextureHandle handle;
     if (gfx::tex_copy_conv::needs_conversion(texCopyFmt)) {
       handle = gfx::new_conv_texture(dstWidth, dstHeight, texCopyFmt, "Copy Conv Texture");
